/--
The unweighted von Mangoldt mass of prime powers at most `x` that are not coprime to `q`; it
bounds the absolute size of the character correction.-/
noncomputable def primePowerCorrectionMass (x q : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 x with IsPrimePow n ∧ ¬Nat.Coprime n q,
    Real.log (n.minFac : ℝ)

/--
Pairs `(p, k)` with `p ∈ q.primeFactors`, `1 ≤ k ≤ x`, and `p^k ≤ x`, indexing the prime-power
contributions excluded by coprimality. In particular, the set is empty when `q = 0`, following
the convention for `Nat.primeFactors`.-/
def primePowerCorrectionPairs (x q : ℕ) : Finset (ℕ × ℕ) :=
  (q.primeFactors ×ˢ Finset.Icc 1 x).filter fun pk => pk.1 ^ pk.2 ≤ x

